# Shared wayside PLC program v1 — identical source on Windows and Raspberry Pi.
# This is the project's bounded Boolean language, not IEC ladder logic or Python.
# The runtime supplies these inputs after evaluating the configured territory:
#   route_safe: candidate route passes occupancy, topology, fault and maintenance checks
#   running: simulation is resumed and maintenance mode is off
#   switch_safe: switch protection zone is clear, current, unreserved and unlocked
#   requested_normal: requested/reported switch position is Normal (false means Reverse)
#   crossing_required: occupied/uncertain approach or protected movement needs gates closed
# Numeric speed/distance calculations and the final independent guard stay in the runtime.

movement_enabled = route_safe and running
allow_route = movement_enabled
signal_clear = movement_enabled

# This output selects a position; it never grants permission to move a switch.
# The runtime separately requires switch_safe before applying the requested position.
switch_normal = requested_normal

# Protective closure remains active while paused or while maintenance mode is on.
crossing_close = crossing_required or not running
